    Bug 1257826 - Fix Sort by Received for search db views. r=tobyp

    When a message header is added to a threaded search db view, its thread is moved to the right place if the view is sorted by date and the message is the newest in that thread. The same happens if the sort order is changed, since the view is rebuilt in this case. Unfortunately this mechanism wasn't enabled when sorting by date received.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D239246

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgSearchDBView.cpp b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgSearchDBView.cpp
index 099eb14aca3..5d8ac2d6fb2 100644
--- a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgSearchDBView.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgSearchDBView.cpp
@@ -462,7 +462,8 @@ nsresult nsMsgSearchDBView::AddHdrFromFolder(nsIMsgDBHdr* msgHdr,
                    "threadRoot incorrect, or level incorrect");

       bool moveThread = false;
-      if (m_sortType == nsMsgViewSortType::byDate) {
+      if (m_sortType == nsMsgViewSortType::byDate ||
+          m_sortType == nsMsgViewSortType::byReceived) {
         uint32_t newestMsgInThread = 0, msgDate = 0;
         viewThread->GetNewestMsgDate(&newestMsgInThread);
         msgHdr->GetDateInSeconds(&msgDate);
